<p>The United States eased sanctions on Belarus after Minsk released 250 political prisoners, the largest such release reported so far. The deal linked humanitarian concessions to economic relief. The Trump administration lifted restrictions on Belarusian fertilizer products and, according to Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty, on several Belarusian entities and the Finance Ministry. The New York Times said the move came as fertilizer prices rose during the Iran war and as Washington pursued a broader rapprochement with Minsk. The agreement opens a rare channel between Washington and Belarusian President Alexander Lukashenko after years of sanctions and isolation. At the same time, the articles make clear that many political prisoners remain behind bars. Opposition figures and rights groups welcomed the releases while pressing for more action.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/BPtrA_E0kyFpliVMb6LChoydD1J95YZ5Q54HYoVwmYy1n7myOTQ5LcCpgaJf_Cuh9jE-BN9og8Sp8Am2qSZWQ21suYIkDK1MR3tS9XtQTen5PvHDK6hE0wVCcbH-FJPPUaLiIRL3H_xRe-7i5fizjWZ9pmqRtyQBzlNsEZRlSf3QfUBguQ' alt='Released human rights defender Valentin Stefanovich faces reporters after arriving in Vilnius after a prisoner release from Belarus on March 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named detainees: Those released included journalist Katsyaryna Andreyeva and political detainee Kim Samusenko, according to RFE/RL.</li><li>Bargaining process: SCMP said the exchange was part of an ongoing negotiation in which Lukashenko sought to normalize ties with Washington after years of isolation and sanctions.</li><li>Market trigger: The New York Times said the Iran war&#x27;s impact on fertilizer prices gave both sides a practical reason to move quickly.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: US officials used targeted sanctions relief as leverage, tying concrete economic concessions to prisoner releases to test a possible thaw with Minsk. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/world/europe/belarus-prisoners-fertilizer-potash-sanctions.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Svetlana Tikhanovskaya: The Belarusian opposition leader publicly thanked President Trump for helping secure the release and used the moment to press for more humanitarian steps. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/20/belarus-frees-250-political-prisoners-in-us-brokered-deal_6751627_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Viasna: The Belarusian human rights group focused on documenting who had been released, grounding outside reporting in prisoner-by-prisoner monitoring as the deal unfolded. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3347236/belarus-frees-250-political-prisoners-us-removes-more-sanctions-latest-signs-thaw'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Deutsche Welle: DW emphasized the scale of the exchange, describing it as a humanitarian breakthrough tied to US sanctions easing, not a wholesale end to repression. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/belarus-releases-250-political-prisoners-as-part-of-us-deal/a-76442237'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/world/europe/belarus-prisoners-fertilizer-potash-sanctions.html'>U.S. Lifts Fertilizer Sanctions on Belarus as Iran War Causes Price Surge</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/belarus-releases-250-political-prisoners-as-part-of-us-deal/a-76442237'>Belarus releases 250 political prisoners as part of US deal</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3347236/belarus-frees-250-political-prisoners-us-removes-more-sanctions-latest-signs-thaw'>Belarus frees 250 political prisoners, US removes more sanctions in latest signs of thaw</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/washington-sanctions-minsk-belarus-prisoners-release/33710939.html'>Washington Eases Sanctions On Minsk As Belarus Releases 250 Prisoners</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/20/belarus-frees-250-political-prisoners-in-us-brokered-deal_6751627_4.html'>Belarus frees 250 political prisoners in US-brokered deal</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>